<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>. ValidationRule.Description is
        capped at 255 characters; a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata
        API. It must sit INSIDE the root element. A comment placed ABOVE <ValidationRule>
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml
        file" error.

        =====================================================================================
        ADDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A1).
        =====================================================================================
        The offer amount is the offer. Everything downstream of this object, the counter
        rounds, Final_Agreed_Price__c, the selected offer and eventually the PSA contract
        value, starts from a number that must exist.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 A VALIDATION RULE, NOT `required=true`. THE SAME MEASURED REASON AS
        BOV_Amount_Required_On_Submission, AND IT DIVERGES FROM THE REQUIREMENTS DOC THE SAME
        WAY. Read that file's header for the full argument; the short form:
        =====================================================================================
        Requirements doc §2 A1 routes both CURRENCY fields to `required=true`. Measured
        2026-08-20, Disposition_Offer__c.Offer_Amount__c is granted EDITABLE in
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit and READABLE in DPEG_Disposition_View. A universally required
        field cannot carry field level security, and the Metadata API rejects a
        fieldPermissions entry naming one, so `required=true` would force both grants to be
        deleted from files this same tranche is editing for an unrelated FLS repair. A rule
        keeps the grants and adds an authored message.

        =====================================================================================
        NO ISCHANGED / ISNEW GUARD. Invariant, not transition. Self clearing.
        ⚠ ZERO, NOT BLANK, IS WHAT THIS RULE DOES NOT TEST. ISBLANK on a Currency field is
        true only for an EMPTY field; a deliberately entered 0 passes here. That is correct
        separation of concerns: "an amount is present" is this rule, "the amount is sane" is
        Counter_Price_Is_Positive's job on the counter fields. There is no positivity rule on
        Offer_Amount__c itself and that omission is deliberate, matching the requirements
        doc's rule inventory. A zero dollar opening offer is unusual but it is a real
        negotiating position, and refusing it would be this file inventing a policy nobody
        asked for.
        =====================================================================================
        MEASURED IMPACT AT CREATION: ZERO ROWS. Queried on usman-dpeg, 2026-08-20:
          SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Disposition_Offer__c                            -> 0
          SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Disposition_Offer__c WHERE Offer_Amount__c = null -> 0
        🔴 That measurement ages; re-run at deploy time.
    -->
    <fullName>Offer_Amount_Required_On_Offer</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>An offer must carry the amount offered. Blocks a blank Offer_Amount__c only; a deliberate zero is permitted, since positivity on the counter fields is Counter_Price_Is_Positive&apos;s job. A rule, not required=true, because required fields cannot hold FLS.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>ISBLANK(Offer_Amount__c)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorMessage>Enter the Offer Amount. An offer with no amount cannot be countered, ranked against the other offers on this disposition, or selected as the winning offer.</errorMessage>
    <errorDisplayField>Offer_Amount__c</errorDisplayField>
</ValidationRule>
